WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:12.460
2. EQ. Having to worry about our IQ is bad enough, and now there's something called

2
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:23.060
an EQ. Do we have to stress about that too? The answer is yes and no. Your EQ stands for

3
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:28.880
Emotional Quotient. It's a measure of how well you understand your own feelings and

4
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.760
those of other people. People with high EQs are very aware of their emotions and those

5
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:41.440
of others. They manage their emotions well. Emotions may not seem to be important for

6
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:48.460
serious life issues like school and work. However, we are discovering that, in fact,

7
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:55.960
having a good understanding of emotions is extremely important in any group situation.

8
00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:02.640
Others are always looking for employees with good people skills, right? Your EQ is just

9
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:09.500
that, your people skills. People with high EQs become influential leaders and helpful

10
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:16.640
managers who understand how to deal with stressed employees. They understand how to use people's

11
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:23.080
feelings to achieve their goals, whether to create trust within a team or create passion

12
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:31.600
for a project. Outside of work, a high EQ is connected to romantic success. Understanding

13
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:38.280
your partner's emotions can certainly help you create a solid relationship. There are many ways

14
00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:45.320
to measure your EQ. Most ask you to perform different emotional problem-solving tasks.

15
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:53.800
Testing your EQ is a useful way to find out how well you read emotions. If you think your EQ

16
00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:00.920
might be low, there are ways to improve it. First, get in touch with your emotions. Think

17
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:07.000
about how they affect your actions. When you feel your emotions leading you to a bad action,

18
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.600
see if you can stop it. Then, concentrate on other people. See if you can identify their

19
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:19.760
emotions and emotional reasons for their actions. In this way, you will build patience,

20
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.800
compassion, and a strong EQ.
